# Laravel 12 & PHP 8.4 Standards

## Code Style & Architecture
- **PHP Version:** PHP 8.4. Use constructor property promotion, strict typing where applicable, typed properties, and explicit return types on methods.
- **Controllers:** Keep controllers thin. Extract business logic into service classes (`app/Services/`).
- **Validation:** Use Form Requests (`app/Http/Requests`) or Livewire validation rules. Do not perform inline controller validation.
- **Database & Eloquent:**
  - Explicitly define relationship return types (`BelongsTo`, `HasMany`, `BelongsToMany`).
  - Maintain `$fillable` on models.
  - Never mutate existing migrations that have run. Always create a new migration for schema changes (`database/migrations/`).
- **Code Style (Pint):** Adhere to the Laravel Pint preset defined in `pint.json`. Verify formatting with `vendor/bin/pint`.

## Command Execution
The host environment may run an older PHP version. Run all commands inside Docker:
```bash
docker compose exec app php artisan <command>
docker compose exec app php artisan test
docker compose exec app php vendor/bin/pint --test
```
